==Appearances in media==
* Kepler-22b is used as:
** A plot device for the 2012 teen science fiction novel ''Kepler 22b'' by Bangladeshi author [[Muhammad Zafar Iqbal]].<ref>{{Cite book |last=Iqbal |first=Muhammed Zafar |title=Kepler 2 2 B |isbn=9788192968568 |language=bn}}</ref>
** A map in Łukasz Jakowski's video games ''Age of Civilizations'' (2014) and ''Age of History II'' (2017, known as ''Age of Civilizations 2'' until 2020). In AoH2, there are 404 provinces that players must control to win the game.{{cn|date=January 2026}}
** The setting for the 2019 children's science fiction book series ''Kepler'' by Sri Lankan author Binendra.{{cn|date=January 2026}}
** The setting for the 2020 U.S. TV series ''[[Raised by Wolves (American TV series)|Raised by Wolves]]'', which was filmed using [[South Africa]] as a substitute for the planet.<ref name=Space-20200903>{{cite news |url= https://www.space.com/raised-by-wolves-hbo-max-episodes-1-2-review.html |title= 'Raised By Wolves' brings Ridley Scott's new sci-fi vision to HBO Max  |first= Scott|last=Snowden |date= 3 September 2020 |publisher= [[Space.com]] }}</ref>
** The title of a song on ''[[Omnium Gatherum (album)|Omnium Gatherum]]'', the 20th studio album by [[King Gizzard & the Lizard Wizard]].
** The source of a radio signal in ''[[Pluribus (TV series)|Pluribus]]'', which contains a recipe for a ribonucleic acid (RNA) sequence.<ref>{{cite web| url=https://decider.com/2025/12/19/pluribus-kepler-22b-planet/| title=What Is Kepler-22b On ‘Pluribus’? What To Know About The Planet That Sent The Radio Signal To Earth| first=Nicole| last=Gallucci| date=19 December 2025| website=decider.com}}</ref>
** The destination of the faster-than-light starship Stalwart II from [[Scott Sigler]]'s short story ''[[Scott Sigler bibliography|The Sadness & Joy]]'' collected in ''[[The Apocalypse Triptych]]'' edited by [[John Joseph Adams]] and [[Hugh Howey]].

